{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha","id":1066944,"title":"[Dark Eras] Forsaken by Rome \u2013 Roman Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T09:29:59-07:00","id":1066944,"title":"[Dark Eras] Forsaken by Rome \u2013 Roman Uratha","content":"So new Dark Era has lore. A LOT of lore. It\u2019s glorious and cool - but somehow I feel it\u2019s to crammed to properly parses it. This topic is to explain all of it, in more friendly take. If you feel I got something wrong, point me where and how so. I will probably do similar thing for Germania Tribes, if feel need for it. So, let\u2019s look over Roman werewolves here\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Origins:</b> Roman Uratha stem from Romulus that with his twin brother Remus where raised by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acca_Larentia\" target=\"_blank\">Acca Larentia</a> \u2013 who was werewomen. As Acca in real world is in different versions saint women, prostitute and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Capitoline Wolf</a> itself \u2013 I certainly can see it all as one Uratha female. Still, weird to me is not saying that Capitoline Wolf is Mother Wolf and Luna is her Mother-Lover that created Uratha in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As both Romulus and Remus were Uratha ( probably by taking it from Acca ), Romulus killed brother in fit of Rage. Now <i>all</i> Roman werewolves say they come from Romulus linage. Particular two great clans comes from them\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Side note:</b> Remus corpses were legendary host for dark forces that pray on living and wanted to go underground Rome at day \u2013 interesting twist in vampires origins. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Next on, Government of Uratha\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-23-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:40:51-07:00","id":1066952,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> o.m.g.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:54:38-07:00","id":1066964,"title":"","content":"<b>Government:</b> Roman Uratha and Wolf-Blooded are split over to two great clans that run Roman Protectorate. First are <i>Saturi</i>, under protection of Ivory Claws, that are entwined with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrician_(ancient_Rome)\" target=\"_blank\">patrician</a> class of Roman citizens. Second are <i>Marisi</i>, under care of Iron Masters, that are connected to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plebs\" target=\"_blank\">plebeian</a> class of society. Both Saturi and Marisi fighted for power with each king chosen from one or another family.<br /> <br /> Finally, at birth of Republic, they made alliance on to make sure that local dispute did not mean end of Roman werewolves blood \u2013 they called their Roman kind as the <i>Urdeshga</i>, and their territories as the Romulan Protectorate. The Urdeshga established the Council of Eagles and Lightning, <i>Concilium Aquilarum et Fulminum</i>, to represent and rule the Protectorate and their families. The Council consists of 12 Saturi <i>Ancilia</i> and 12 Marisi <i>Salii</i> \u2014 each respected and politically powerful within their family, and usually of advanced age. Non-Urdeshga can only become \u2018associated member\u2019 \u2013 called <i>Foederati</i> \u2013 but only by loyalty to one Council member. Outside of official Council protection in Romulan Protectorate you can become pray to any member Hunts.<br /> <br /> Next on, Shadow Realm of Rome\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-23-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:04:17-07:00","id":1066969,"title":"","content":"<b>Shadow Realm:</b> Roman Uratha call their spirits as two tiers \u2013 low Ranks ( Rank 1-3, I assume ) are <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lares\" target=\"_blank\">Lares</a>, </i>household personal spirits. High Ranks ( Rank 4-5 ) are called <i>Maters</i> and took the names and forms of Rome\u2019s gods. In 205 BCE, the Senate sent for a statue of Cybele from Pergamon and with it came <i>Magna Mater</i> \u2013 great Shadow goddess that quickly become patron of Rome itself. But something was wrong with Magna\u2026<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Council of Eagles and Lighting had totems, of course, of Eagle and Lighting. By centuries it evolved into coherent spirit-symbol of Roman conquest and Legions, known as <i>Aquilae</i>. And this is how it looks:<br /> <img src=\"http://www.figurines-12-pouces.com/12649-23163-thickbox_default/roman-legion-aquila.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <b>Hathis-Ur</b>: I still do not understand who is Hathis-Ur \u2013 and checked specifically both 1E and 2E corebooks for term. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Someone can help on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:13:39-07:00","id":1066975,"title":"","content":"Hathis-Ur is the First Tongue name for Silver Wolf, patron of the Ivory Claws. I find it interesting that the high-Rank <i>Maters </i>of the Roman Shadow actively take the name and image of their gods, but it isn't all that surprising when you think about it. Now, Cybele, I find very intriguing. The name <i>Magna Mater</i> would suggest she is Rank 6 at least. What appears to be the problem with this spirit? Insane like Irnanim the Colossus or secretly an Idigam?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:24:56-07:00","id":1066988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1066975#post1066975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Cybele, I find very intriguing. The name <i>Magna Mater</i> would suggest she is Rank 6 at least. What appears to be the problem with this spirit? Insane like Irnanim the Colossus or secretly an Idigam?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will not say anything here... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:12:49-07:00","id":1067022,"title":"","content":"I'm salivating over this. I knew Forsaken by Rome would make me a Werewolf fanboy but I never knew how much.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ...how long before this becomes available to the general public again???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:15:45-07:00","id":1067025,"title":"","content":"A few weeks to get errata, maybe a month for finishing touches. I've no idea.<br /> <br /> It's definitely my favorite Dark Era now, very well done. I loved the Sundered World but only really for the werewolf section. I was hesitant way before because it was implied to be just about the barbarian werewolves under Rome's rule, and figured it would dismiss the werewolves as woodland savages or something, though nikink helped dissuade me of that. I was worried when I first started reading and saw it hinged on, basically, a single act, but it's great. It's definitely going to be fun to play, I love the use of protectorates, especially Pure and Forsaken ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:53:18-07:00","id":1067115,"title":"","content":"I'm more frustrated than I should be at how little the Magna Mater in the text resembles the historical Magna Mater. There's a token reference to its origin as being bound within a statue of Cybele, but none of the actual details on her role as a fertility deity out of Anatolia, or the super interesting detail that her cult consisted largely of self-castrated men who lived as women.<br /> <br /> Why bother drawing on the name of a historical cult if you're not gonna use it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:00:18-07:00","id":1067121,"title":"","content":"Probably because the name was just usurped by Shar-Z\u2019ghub. The goddess existed before it even came into play.<br /> <br /> There's also the point that most of the era takes place outside of Rome itself, focusing on the legions and the night and day tribes.<br /> <br /> The idigam itself seems ambiguous so you can do what you want to it in case your own game heads back to the capitol, either with the Germanic tribes taking the war there or Romans arriving as victors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:14:37-07:00","id":1067127,"title":"","content":"Of course it's an idigam. Knew it had to be an idigam, the whole &quot;mother&quot; aspect of it suggests the Forge Servant Dread Powers. Only question is, is it Earthbound or did it Coalesce later, since I seem to recall a notable effigy of Cybele being made from a meteor of some kind (which the idigam could have rode in on or Coalesced around).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:17:12-07:00","id":1067128,"title":"","content":"It's called an Earth-bound, it seems a bit more like the Earth-bound of Demon the Fallen. But it's sort of anchored in a piece of meteoric stone, yes the one you're thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:29:20-07:00","id":1067140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067115#post1067115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more frustrated than I should be at how little the Magna Mater in the text resembles the historical Magna Mater. There's a token reference to its origin as being bound within a statue of Cybele, but none of the actual details on her role as a fertility deity out of Anatolia, or the super interesting detail that her cult consisted largely of self-castrated men who lived as women.<br /> <br /> Why bother drawing on the name of a historical cult if you're not gonna use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only because we didn't have the space. Believe me we would have LOVED to expand on... basically everything. As it was tons of stuff was already cut away. Sorry!<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:33:55-07:00","id":1067144,"title":"","content":"To expand on what wyrdhamster's posted, Rome is a protectorate led by Iron Masters and Ivory Claws. Other members can be part of it but they're never 'true' Roman and usually are put into the military.<br /> <br /> The era is based around the war with the Germanic tribes, the Legion being sort of led on by a wolf-blooded hostage, born of Germani but raised in Rome, who sees the Roman Protectorate as corrupt and seeks to unite the tribes of Germani to fight against it and, potentially, destroy it. Most of the era is focused around that and the results of it. There's protectorates among the Germanic tribes, too like the Brekan Protectorate of Blood Talon packs, and the Hercynian Protectorate of Bone Shadows and Predator Kings and I realize using the term tribe so much might be confusing. The focus is most obviously on the Roman Protectorate.<br /> <br /> It looks like a lot of fun, and a <i>lot </i>of chaos. Which is appropriate for a war where such stakes are on the line. Reading the section about Rome's Revenge, I actually said, 'oh shit,' at the thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:13:48-07:00","id":1067167,"title":"","content":"So, sorry if this is a dumb question, but what exactly <i>is</i> this? Is it like a book, or a section from a book...it sounds <i>really</i> interesting, and I'm <b>super</b> into <i>WtF</i> lately so I'm actually in the market for as much 2E <i>WtF</i> stuff as I can get. I know some of the Dark Eras that are being released are individual sections from the big Dark Eras book that came out a little while ago, but this sounds like it's new. (or supplementary to that)<br /> <br /> Otherwise, this is all really cool. Rome is such an interesting era (or series of eras, since it covers so much time), as a time when a single civilization united (or at least &quot;united&quot;) such a wide swathe of diverse territories and cultures. Lots of potential, there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:16:23-07:00","id":1067171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067167#post1067167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, sorry if this is a dumb question, but what exactly <i>is</i> this? Is it like a book, or a section from a book...it sounds <i>really</i> interesting, and I'm <b>super</b> into <i>WtF</i> lately so I'm actually in the market for as much 2E <i>WtF</i> stuff as I can get. I know some of the Dark Eras that are being released are individual sections from the big Dark Eras book that came out a little while ago, but this sounds like it's new. (or supplementary to that)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of the Dark Eras Companion, a supplement that was funded along the Dark Eras book that has been already published. It includes several new chapters, Forsaken By Rome being one of those.<br /> <br /> Those who pledged to the Kickstarter got the link to the advance copy today, but it will be eventually be released to the wider public as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:16:34-07:00","id":1067172,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras was a <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Kickstarter project</a>, and it ended up getting so much support that the content wouldn't fit in one book. So they split it into two, Dark Eras and the Dark Eras Companion. The Dark Eras Companion was just let out to the Kickstarter backers earlier today, and the second chapter is devoted to werewolf, called Forsaken by Rome. Odds are the Forsaken by Rome Era would be sold on its own at a much later date, and the Companion on its own in a couple months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:51:34-07:00","id":1067217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067140#post1067140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only because we didn't have the space. Believe me we would have LOVED to expand on... basically everything. As it was tons of stuff was already cut away. Sorry!<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a possibility we could see all that stuff in the boards or in the blogs or wherever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:07:32-07:00","id":1067224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067172#post1067172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eras was a <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Kickstarter project</a>, and it ended up getting so much support that the content wouldn't fit in one book. So they split it into two, Dark Eras and the Dark Eras Companion. The Dark Eras Companion was just let out to the Kickstarter backers earlier today, and the second chapter is devoted to werewolf, called Forsaken by Rome. Odds are the Forsaken by Rome Era would be sold on its own at a much later date, and the Companion on its own in a couple months.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! Is there a list of all the Dark Eras done so far? (especially those in 2e) The Kickstarter link has the ones in the book, but either the Companion eras aren't listed there or I didn't look hard enough. (I <i>am</i> at work &gt;_&gt;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:19:26-07:00","id":1067227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067224#post1067224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! Is there a list of all the Dark Eras done so far? (especially those in 2e) The Kickstarter link has the ones in the book, but either the Companion eras aren't listed there or I didn't look hard enough. (I <i>am</i> at work &gt;_&gt;)</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, I had a hard time finding them too. <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1173741\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link</a>.<br /> <br /> And here's a list.<br /> <br /> Second Sight: Age of Spiritualism<br /> Demon: Russian Revolution<br /> Mummy: Cleopatran Egypt<br /> Promethean: Year Without a Summer<br /> Geist: Roanoke<br /> Werewolf: Forsaken by Rome<br /> Mage: Mutapan Empire (backer resurrected era) - This is shared with Mummy.<br /> Promethean: Black Death (backer resurrected era) - This has Vampire too.<br /> Promethean: 30 Years War (backer suggested era)<br /> <br /> Beast also got an American Reconstruction Era Dark Era as part of Beast's Kickstarter, and it is in the Companion. It takes place from 1863-1865.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:34:48-07:00","id":1067285,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Is this some backer early stuff which you're summarizing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:40:33-07:00","id":1067360,"title":"","content":"That setting is fucking great!!! I just have read the Roman history section and, although Werewolf is not among my fav games (nothing against it, it's just not my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), Im loving it more and more. The setting is just great and the change in the Uratha society is marvelous (that's one of the thngs I love more, the Uratha having a very politized and hierarchised society).<br /> <br /> Things that Im thinking just now:<br /> 1) It's sad the history ends around 15-20 CE. I'd love to see how roman uratha society would evolve during the Roman Empire.<br /> 2) I absolutelly need a roman mage setting. <br /> 3) In conclusion: Id love a roman historical gameline that extends unitil the fall of Rome. With Requiem for Rome Revised, Werewolf expanded to fall of Rome (and with full splats for the Tribes and the Council) and a setting for Rome, explaining the institutionalization of Darshanas into Orders.<br /> <br /> Great job, folks!!!!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian 