tar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:18:53-07:00","id":1067409,"title":"","content":"Also: YES! I would KILL (like, seriously kill) to write more Roman settings!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:39:08-07:00","id":1067677,"title":"","content":"Really exceptional setting. I didn't think it'd be among my favourites, but here we are... It's really, really cool.<br /> <br /> Great job, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2653\" data-vbnamecard=\"2653\">NateD</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:14:56-07:00","id":1067903,"title":"","content":"Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And don't forget Bunyip also wrote for that setting - a triumvirate!)<br /> <br /> And to echo Nate, I'd love to write more about the whole setting. I had a mental picture of events and migrations and state of the world snapshots that led from the Sundered World setting through Sumeria, through the bronze age collapse, around the Mediterranean, into Italy and subsequently to Rome and Carthage. Also from the Balkans, Black Sea, through to Scandinavia and northern Europe, Albion and Iberia. And all (well, a lot of) the knock on effects and how they all became the FbR setting.<br /> <br /> I'd love to write more about any and all of that. That's not up to me though, it's in the hands of fans and Devs and OPP and WWP. And to be clear, that's not material I wrote and subsequently got cut - it was a mental model with some dot points and references to keep straight. It informed what was written and some of that then got cut.<br /> <br /> And that's the broad strokes. Every step of the way was filled with details that I'd've loved to expand upon, like Lex's Magna Mater mortal cult. The history of Rome was over stuffed with wonderful details. God it was hard to rein it in to leave space for the wonders of the Germanic Uratha. (The writer's lament) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:28:04-07:00","id":1067905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067903#post1067903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And don't forget Bunyip also wrote for that setting - a triumvirate!)<br /> <br /> And to echo Nate, I'd love to write more about the whole setting. I had a mental picture of events and migrations and state of the world snapshots that led from the Sundered World setting through Sumeria, through the bronze age collapse, around the Mediterranean, into Italy and subsequently to Rome and Carthage. Also from the Balkans, Black Sea, through to Scandinavia and northern Europe, Albion and Iberia. And all (well, a lot of) the knock on effects and how they all became the FbR setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I have to admit I'm more than a little curious about your ideas for the Bronze Age Collapse. It's not every day you have multiple superpowers of a complex, cosmopolitan section of the world simultaneously go down in flames due to migrant groups that apparently came from nowhere and then vanished into thin air. Looking at you Sea Peoples, looking at you.<br /> <br /> Also, the presence of the <i>Mater </i>in the Eternal City itself gets me to thinking if that is relatively... standard for the much more strongly polytheistic and animistic past of the CofD. There obviously won't be one spirit that happens to be Zeus/Jupiter anymore than there is one Goetic that is Zeus/Jupiter (though there's probably an Ur-Zeus that amalgamates them all). Closest thing I can think of is The Thunderer in Summoners, who is Rank 6 at least and is more Chalcolithic/Early Bronze Age than anything else. But that's besides the point. Do you guys think that the largest major metropolitan centres would have powerful spirits, possibly Rank 4-5, reflecting the gods worshipped in the city?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I can absolutely say I want more. You guys keep writing spectacular Dark Eras, and this antiquities/anthropology nerd will keep buying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T21:35:02-07:00","id":1067916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067903#post1067903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And don't forget Bunyip also wrote for that setting - a triumvirate!)<br /> <br /> And to echo Nate, I'd love to write more about the whole setting. I had a mental picture of events and migrations and state of the world snapshots that led from the Sundered World setting through Sumeria, through the bronze age collapse, around the Mediterranean, into Italy and subsequently to Rome and Carthage. Also from the Balkans, Black Sea, through to Scandinavia and northern Europe, Albion and Iberia. And all (well, a lot of) the knock on effects and how they all became the FbR setting.<br /> <br /> I'd love to write more about any and all of that. That's not up to me though, it's in the hands of fans and Devs and OPP and WWP. And to be clear, that's not material I wrote and subsequently got cut - it was a mental model with some dot points and references to keep straight. It informed what was written and some of that then got cut.<br /> <br /> And that's the broad strokes. Every step of the way was filled with details that I'd've loved to expand upon, like Lex's Magna Mater mortal cult. The history of Rome was over stuffed with wonderful details. God it was hard to rein it in to leave space for the wonders of the Germanic Uratha. (The writer's lament) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I...NEEED... THIIIIS....<br /> <br /> Please. Include all of this in Dark Eras 2. Or in a book that details Uratha history similar to the future Tome of the Pentacle from Mage)... ir wherever!!!<br /> But please, write this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T22:26:14-07:00","id":1067921,"title":"","content":"Oh yes! Things I'd have loved to expand upon:<br /> <br /> - Magna Mater - both the spirit itself, the other Maters, and the historical Cybelline cult (and ya'll were right; namechecking Cybele was totally inspired by *that* stone, but that wasn't all there was to it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />);<br /> <br /> - Rome itself! Unfortunately, it was a little beyond our remit here, but I'd have *loved* to explore more of Rome through the Uratha's eyes. I have a character that I've been dying to put into something published, but unfortunately there just wasn't space.<br /> <br /> - the fall of the Romulan Protectorate - I don't really have to explain that, do I? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - life for the Germanic Uratha - I was really intrigued by the practicalities of Uratha life when you're so spread out, the mortal culture around you is large family unit-based, and your territory is in an area where a lot of (often nomadic, or at least migratory) mortal tribes intermingle.<br /> <br /> So in short - yes! There's so much more we would have LOVED to write!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T22:27:10-07:00","id":1067922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067903#post1067903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to echo Nate, I'd love to write more about the whole setting. I had a mental picture of events and migrations and state of the world snapshots that led from the Sundered World setting through Sumeria, through the bronze age collapse, around the Mediterranean,</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that Sumeria would be place where the Tribes of Moon - as Oaths bound alliance - would be created? And the Gods of Bau... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo