0","id":1067944,"title":"","content":"Welp, I live in hope of being able to expand on it all. I think the splitting of the Urdeshga would be fascinating to delve into. the rise and rise of the Saturi, the 'night of long claws' to destroy the Marisi and expel them from the Council of Eagles and Lightning, the descent of the Council into a lodge as the Empire rises and falls. The alliances and common ground found with the Firetouched and Predator Kings while the Marisi bond with their cousins until the name 'Marisi' itself is shunned and forgotten.<br /> <br /> Almost makes me feel bad for the Iron Masters - going from Mediterranean top-dogs around the Bronze Age, to rising with the Roman Republic, to splitting from the cunning Saturi, and dwindling throughout the Roman Empire's life. But they are nothing if not adaptable! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T01:33:09-07:00","id":1067945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067398#post1067398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Dark Eras 2 doesn't have Changeling in Britannia and Promethean in Judea I'm going to cry.<br /> <br /> Also, I cannot wait to steal a bunch of material from Cthulhu Invictus 7e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be SO DOWN for both of these! <br /> <br /> There's a lot that can be done with 1st century Judea, too - all the biblical dead-raising is obvious (Lazarus, come forth!), but the pseudo-gnostic writers of the Dead Sea Scrolls (the Essenes, I believe? It's been a little while) would work *so well*. They had good and evil angels, purification, (potential) influences from cthonic mystery cults, and they literally &quot;went to the wastes&quot;.<br /> <br /> And if you love Oscar Wilde's Salome as much as I do, you'd have possibly thought that everyone's reaction to Jokaanan / John the Baptist (who it seems was taught by the DSS writers) always seemed a little...disquieting.<br /> <br /> And that's not even mentioning all the other self-proclaimed prophets, saviors, revolutionaries and angel-whisperers of the time. <br /> <br /> Seriously, I could write a hell of a lot for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T01:59:57-07:00","id":1067947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067905#post1067905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the presence of the <i>Mater </i>in the Eternal City itself gets me to thinking if that is relatively... standard for the much more strongly polytheistic and animistic past of the CofD. There obviously won't be one spirit that happens to be Zeus/Jupiter anymore than there is one Goetic that is Zeus/Jupiter (though there's probably an Ur-Zeus that amalgamates them all). Closest thing I can think of is The Thunderer in Summoners, who is Rank 6 at least and is more Chalcolithic/Early Bronze Age than anything else. But that's besides the point. Do you guys think that the largest major metropolitan centres would have powerful spirits, possibly Rank 4-5, reflecting the gods worshipped in the city?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has given me a lot to think about. I like the idea of there being many Zeuses/Jupiters in any given cities. Roman religion would actually <i>support </i>you in that theory, given that they often had &quot;The Jupiter of X City&quot; and &quot;The Jupiter of the Old River&quot; and so on. There may be one central Zeus the Olympian, Son of Cronus, but his Rank is surely 9-10 and beyond mortal reckoning. But it definitely allows you to actually have the PCs encounter Gods in the game at Rank 5 or 6, given that these Gods are not the ur-God, but rather merely a reflection of the God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:09:05-07:00","id":1067965,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, totally. Apart from spirits of Faith itself (which would no doubt be flavoured by the particular faith they're born / feed from), there would be spirits of various revered phenomena and places that have been coloured by mortal ideas. Personally, I'd consider leaving it unclear how much is really &quot;them&quot;, and how much is a kind of natural camouflage - if you look like the local mortals' idea of a fire god, for example, you'll get a lot of fires burned in your name.<br /> <br /> Then there's, uh, what are they called again - Royal Avatars, perhaps? Shards of Rank 6+ spirits, which may well be the capital &quot;g&quot; Gods of Shadow. Maybe that is what &quot;real&quot; Zeus is, and each Rank 5 Zeus people have encountered is just a shard of the whole?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the CoD is positively lousy with gods, and I love that. I feel it fits perfectly with WtF's animism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:30:37-07:00","id":1068795,"title":"","content":"I can't help but thinking Rats in the Walls when reading about the Magna Mater cult.<br /> I dunno, but this feels more connected to Lovecraft's view of the cult, than the actual historical one.<br /> <br /> Which, I might add, I'm completely fine with!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067965#post1067965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, totally. Apart from spirits of Faith itself (which would no doubt be flavoured by the particular faith they're born / feed from), there would be spirits of various revered phenomena and places that have been coloured by mortal ideas. Personally, I'd consider leaving it unclear how much is really &quot;them&quot;, and how much is a kind of natural camouflage - if you look like the local mortals' idea of a fire god, for example, you'll get a lot of fires burned in your name.<br /> <br /> Then there's, uh, what are they called again - Royal Avatars, perhaps? Shards of Rank 6+ spirits, which may well be the capital &quot;g&quot; Gods of Shadow. Maybe that is what &quot;real&quot; Zeus is, and each Rank 5 Zeus people have encountered is just a shard of the whole?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the CoD is positively lousy with gods, and I love that. I feel it fits perfectly with WtF's animism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've personally always run it such that gods with actual names are either Astral beings, Fey, or powerful main-splat supers who rule over mortals.<br /> Spirits are a bit too.. Primal for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> My path to Zeus would be something like this:<br /> Mortal shaman witnesses the Dihir Host of Storms, as he rages around the slopes of Olympus.<br /> The shaman then returns to her tribe and tells them about the storm god who rules there.<br /> Over the centuries, after a few more events where they see it, they build up a mythology that humanizes the spirit-god.<br /> Awakened Exarch-cultists sees the symbols related to the General in this being, and push on the deification.<br /> Host of Storms, meanwhile has picked up on the Essence from all the sacrifices to placate it, and has gotten less of a raging monster, and more of a ruler, it's nature changing into Tyrant of Storms.<br /> Anyone who were to visit the Spirit reflection of Olympus would see this spirit, and see the aspects of Zeus in it, but would also see that it isn't the exact same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:47:34-07:00","id":1068854,"title":"","content":"I really love this era. I feel bad because I'm not asking questions but everything was summed up pretty well.<br /> <br /> Reading it, the big question that came up is, 'What happened to the Lodge of the Final Breath?' But it was answered in a sidebar.<br /> <br /> I especially like the ghost legions idea, and the curse of the Rhine and the Mothers in the Wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:55:05-07:00","id":1068916,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://static1.gamespot.com/uploads/original/90/908941/2940116-cac.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">asdasdasdasdasdsdasdasdasdasdasd</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:55:26-07:00","id":1068997,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I had a ball writing The Mothers. Didn't even realise until recently that they literally have THE SAME NAME as the Romulan Protectorate's Maters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:56:35-07:00","id":1068998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1068795#post1068795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but thinking Rats in the Walls when reading about the Magna Mater cult.<br /> I dunno, but this feels more connected to Lovecraft's view of the cult, than the actual historical one.<br /> <br /> Which, I might add, I'm completely fine with!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've personally always run it such that gods with actual names are either Astral beings, Fey, or powerful main-splat supers who rule over mortals.<br /> Spirits are a bit too.. Primal for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> My path to Zeus would be something like this:<br /> Mortal shaman witnesses the Dihir Host of Storms, as he rages around the slopes of Olympus.<br /> The shaman then returns to her tribe and tells them about the storm god who rules there.<br /> Over the centuries, after a few more events where they see it, they build up a mythology that humanizes the spirit-god.<br /> Awakened Exarch-cultists sees the symbols related to the General in this being, and push on the deification.<br /> Host of Storms, meanwhile has picked up on the Essence from all the sacrifices to placate it, and has gotten less of a raging monster, and more of a ruler, it's nature changing into Tyrant of Storms.<br /> Anyone who were to visit the Spirit reflection of Olympus would see this spirit, and see the aspects of Zeus in it, but would also see that it isn't the exact same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve of all of this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:59:17-07:00","id":1068999,"title":"","content":"Also, can I just say that the OPP fans are the bestest! Ya'll have no idea how awesome it is to have people like something you've written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, since no one else has mentioned it yet - DAT ART! I'm of course biased, but the one page spread that goes with the Forsaken by Rome opening fiction is positively mesmerising!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T20:07:32-07:00","id":1069000,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah