s":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T22:13:32-07:00","id":1070486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1069444#post1069444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked that, too, and took it to mean they split up but for some reason the idea of them both serving the same totem appeals too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that there has been a schism by modern times, and I can easily see the foundation cracking as the magath 'Maters' split into decedent choirs. Jupiter <i>Lucetius</i> vs Jupiter Rector, as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:31:10-07:00","id":1071444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067360#post1067360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That setting is fucking great!!! I just have read the Roman history section and, although Werewolf is not among my fav games (nothing against it, it's just not my game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), Im loving it more and more. The setting is just great and the change in the Uratha society is marvelous (that's one of the thngs I love more, the Uratha having a very politized and hierarchised society).<br /> <br /> Things that Im thinking just now:<br /> 1) It's sad the history ends around 15-20 CE. I'd love to see how roman uratha society would evolve during the Roman Empire.<br /> 2) I absolutelly need a roman mage setting.<br /> 3) In conclusion: Id love a roman historical gameline that extends unitil the fall of Rome. With Requiem for Rome Revised, Werewolf expanded to fall of Rome (and with full splats for the Tribes and the Council) and a setting for Rome, explaining the institutionalization of Darshanas into Orders.<br /> <br /> Great job, folks!!!!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067363#post1067363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes Uxas, join me and Atamajakki in the cry for a Roman setting for every game line!!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1066944-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-\u2013-roman-uratha?p=1067409#post1067409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: YES! I would KILL (like, seriously kill) to write more Roman settings!!</div> </div> </div> </div>...hmm.<br /> <br /> &quot;Awakened by Rome&quot; (Mage)<br /> &quot;Created by Rome&quot; (Promethean)<br /> &quot;Lost from Rome&quot; (Changeling)<br /> &quot;Vigil of Rome&quot; (Hunter)<br /> &quot;Bound to Rome&quot; (Geist)<br /> &quot;Curse of Rome&quot; (Mummy)<br /> &quot;Descent of Rome&quot; (Demon)<br /> &quot;Begotten by Rome&quot; (Beast)<br /> &quot;Renegades of Rome&quot; (Deviant)<br /> <br /> Yeah, works pretty well, all considering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:23:56-07:00","id":1092417,"title":"","co