by Luna, as their 'godmother', when Mars did not approve them. Maybe God of War did not like their Death Rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:21:37-07:00","id":1484039,"title":"","content":"I have recently finished reading this chapter, which I enjoyed so much that I want to congratulate the authors. It is a worthy prequel of Requiem of Rome and Fall of the Camarilla, which I already have storytelled. The only thing I did not liked was the evil spirit in the Cibeles statue, I would like a more mundane corruption, being pride and arrogance the true seeds of the fall of Rome, not a demon. This would have give a more humane focus to the plot. I also find equally interesting and hard to implement the rules for a mixed pack of Iron masters and Ivory claws. While the two main barbaric tribes are forsaken, the roman tribes not, and this makes a bit more difficult the process of character creation to play as romans. Anyway, thanks a lot for writting a roman setting for werewolf, Rome is always interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T20:35:19-07:00","id":1485876,"title":"","content":"Huh. Glad you liked it. <img src=\"https://forum.th